n:** Lemma\u202f3 \u2013 \u201cthe condition \\(|B-A|=1\\) together with \\(\\gcd(A,B)=1\\) forces \\(A=-B\\); otherwise the step \\((B,-A)\\) would change the sum \\(a+b\\) by \\(\\pm1\\) while moving one coordinate by at least\u202f2, which would leave the triangle after fewer than \\(t+1\\) steps.\u201d  \n  **Issue:** The deduction that \\(|B-A|=1\\) forces \\(A=-B\\) is incorrect (e.g. \\((A,B)=(2,3)\\) gives \\(|B-A|=1\\) but \\(A\\neq -B\\)). **Critical Error.**\n\n* **Location:** Lemma\u202f4 \u2013 \u201cAdd any sunny line through \\((1,n)\\) (for instance \\(y=2x-1\\)).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** The line \\(y=2x-1\\) passes through \\((1,1)\\), not \\((1,n)\\) for \\(n\\ge3\\); the example is factually wrong. **Critical Error.**\n\n* **Location:** Lemma\u202f4 \u2013 \u201cThe three sunny lines  \n  \\(\\ell_1: y=2x-1,\\; \\ell_2: y=3x-2,\\; \\ell_3: y=5x-4\\) \u2026 cover the whole set \\(T_3'\\).\u201d  \n  **Issue:** None of these lines contain the required points of \\(T_3'\\) (e.g. \\((1,n-2)\\) is not on any of them); the claimed covering is false. **Critical Error.**\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Verification Log\n\n### 1. Definition of \\(T_n\\) and \\(N_n\\)\n\n> \u201cLet  \n> \\[\n> T_n=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z^2\\mid a\\ge1,\\;b\\ge1,\\;a+b\\le n+1\\},\n> \\qquad N_n:=|T_n|=\\frac{n(n+1)}2 .\n> \\]\u201d\n\n*Correct.*  The set \\(T_n\\) is exactly the integer lattice points in the right\u2011angled triangle with vertices \\((1,1),(1,n),(n,1)\\).  Its cardinality is the triangular number \\(\\frac{n(n+1)}2\\).  No issue here.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Lemma\u202f1 \u2013 Maximum number of points of \\(T_n\\) on a sunny line\n\n> \u201cWrite a sunny line as \\(Ax+By=C\\) with integers \\(A,B\\) satisfying (S).  \n> All integer points on the line are \\((a_0,b_0)+t\\,(B,-A),\\;t\\in\\mathbb Z\\).  \n> Hence the sum \\(a+b\\) changes by \\(\\Delta:=B-A\\neq0\\).  \n> Inside \\(T_n\\) we have \\(2\\le a+b\\le n+1\\); therefore the number of admissible values of\n> \\(t\\)